# Proving Ground - BONANZA's course 0, the benchmark's (SPEC.md 128.10.11.1).
#
# Wave 0b's generated test course (SPEC.md 128.3) - a start plateau, a long
# descent with a rail, a landing, a traverse left with a block, a climb, a
# plateau, a sprint down and a finish - in the text format, changed where
# physics v1 needs it:
#  - every ramp a whole half unit a tile, inside the limits;
#  - NARROWER: a NEAR void cell reaches two tiles past a solid one in wx AND
#    wy, four in a = wx - wy, and every reachable footprint must lie inside
#    the 512 px picture, so solid tiles keep to a = -10 .. 10 (wave 0b's
#    spanned -15 .. 16);
#  - the LANDING is a square plateau in the middle of the picture: with the
#    course that narrow GLIDE has only 24 columns to pan in and is clamped at
#    either end of every long leg, so the benchmark's diagonal pans come from
#    the autopilot's loop round the landing (the route below);
#  - every step between floors the route crosses is level or a ramp (a half
#    unit at a ramp's foot is 4.25 px to the floor function, over BZ_CLIMB),
#    and the pits are off the route.
course BENCH "Proving Ground"
width  64

# A. the start plateau, upper left, and its rail
floor rect   5 13  8 16  flat 30
wall  rect   5 12  8 13  flat 32
# B. the descent, down-right along +wx: 30 -> 27.5 over 5 tiles (r = -1)
floor rect   8 13 13 16  ramp x 8 13 30 27.5
wall  rect   8 12 13 13  ramp x 8 13 32 29.5     # its back rail, 2 units proud
# C. the landing: an 8 x 8 plateau level with the descent's foot, and its rail
floor rect  13 13 21 21  flat 27.5
wall  rect  13 12 21 13  flat 29.5
# D. the traverse left, down-left along +wy (r = -1), its back rail, a block
#    beside it the ball rolls behind, and the turn
floor rect  17 21 20 27  ramp y 21 27 27.5 24.5
wall  rect  16 21 17 27  ramp y 21 27 29.5 26.5
wall  tile  19 24        ramp y 21 27 29.5 26.5
floor rect  18 27 20 29  flat 24.5
# E. the climb, back down-right along +wx: 24.5 -> 28.5 over 8 tiles (r = 1)
floor rect  20 26 28 29  ramp x 20 28 24.5 28.5
# F. the plateau at the top of the climb
floor rect  28 25 33 31  flat 28.5
wall  rect  28 24 33 25  flat 30.5
# G. the sprint down: a screen-vertical band, one half unit a tile of s down
#    (wave 0b's ran 56 rows of s; this one 28, so the part fits: SPEC.md
#    128.10.4.2 - the benchmark's 1,200 frames never reach it)
floor band  -1 6  64 92  ramp s 64 92 28.5 14.5
# H. the finish: a wide plateau and a chequered line
floor band  -7 7  92 112 flat 14.5
goal  band  -7 7 102 104 flat 14.5
wall  band  -8 -8 92 112 flat 16.5
wall  band   8  8 92 112 flat 16.5

# pits, off the autopilot's route
hole  tile  10 15
hole  tile  31 30
hole  band  4 4 74 75
hole  band  0 0 84 85

start 6 14

# The benchmark's route (the autopilot, SPEC.md 128.6): the ball's picture
# top-left on each tile's centre, in order, the first the start (bz_play
# begins at the second).  Chosen with a host model of GLIDE driving
# bbcourse.Physics (written to choose, not kept, SPEC.md 128.10.11.1): down the
# descent onto the landing, a loop round it with two reversals, into the
# traverse behind its block, then on toward the climb.  Every one of the
# eight scroll directions occurs at least 8 times on both cards at step rates
# 0.96 - 1.04 of the real one (ten phases each), at least 3 times at 0.92 -
# 0.96; past 1.04 the CGA's up-left and down-left pans can vanish.  The
# 1,200 frames reach the first twelve (the CGA's 1,093 steps) with no fall in
# the Hercules's 1,289; `bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 8 holds that.
way   6 14
way  16 14
way  17 18
way  19 21
way  20 16
way  19 19
way  15 20
way  15 13
way  13 13
way  17 13
way  17 24
way  19 22
way  19 28
way  27 27
way  30 27
